---
title: 40-Clove Garlic Chicken
servings: 4
tags: alcohol
source.author: Tasty.co
source.url: https://tasty.co/recipe/40-clove-garlic-chicken
course: Main dish
prep time: 20 min
cook time: 45 min
nutrition:
  calories: 330 calories
  fat: 12 grams fat
  carbohydrates: 12 grams carbohydrates
  sugar: 5 grams sugar
  protein: 38 grams protein
---

Pre-heat the oven to 350°F.

Season the @chicken{4}(thighs, bone-in) with the @salt, @pepper and @mixed herbs{}(to taste). Set aside.

Heat some oil in a large pan and sear the chicken for about ~{10-15%minutes} evenly on each side, until golden brown.

Take the chicken out and set aside.

Add the @shallots{4}(chopped) and cook down in the remaining juices for about ~{5%minutes} over a low-medium heat.

Add the @garlic cloves{1%bulb}(separated, peeled) and gently cook them for about ~{2%minutes}.

Pour in the @vermouth{1/2%cup}(or white wine) and gently cook so that it reduces slightly.

Add the chicken, @parsley{3%sprigs} and @tarragon{1%tsp}(dried), followed by the @chicken stock{3/4%cup}(low-sodium).

Bake in the oven for ~{20-25%minutes} or until the chicken is cooked through.

= Serving =

Serve with @crusty bread{} and @vegetables of your choice.
